export const DeadmanCopy = {
  TITLE: 'Welcome to Deadman: Annihilation!',
  PAGE1:
    'Deadman is a <col=ffffff>time-limited game mode</col>. Everyone starts with a <col=ffffff>fresh save</col> which can only be used on a Deadman: Annihilation world. Beware of other players, for the <col=ffffff>majority of Gielinor is dangerous</col>!<br><br>The aim of Deadman is to <col=ffffff>acquire Deadman Points</col> which can be used to purchase <col=ffffff>rewards in the main game</col> at the end of the event. You can find more detail on <col=ffffff>how to earn Deadman Points</col> by <col=ffffff>clicking the Skull icon</col><br>under the Quest tab.<br><br>To begin your journey in Deadman, use the <col=ffffff>Get Started</col> button below. Otherwise you can use the <col=ffffff>Exit</col> button to logout.',
  PAGE2:
    "<col=ffffff>Experience</col> gained in Deadman is significantly boosted. <col=ffffff>Drop rates</col> of unique items are also <col=ffffff>significantly buffed</col>. Some <col=ffffff>quests are completed automatically</col> upon logging in.<br><br>In <col=ffffff>guarded areas</col>, other players <col=ffffff>can't attack you</col>. Guarded areas are indicated by a red circle over the skull icon.<br><br><col=ffffff>Logging out</col> outside of a guarded area will take <col=ffffff>7 seconds</col>. <col=ffffff>Teleporting</col> when skulled will also take <col=ffffff>7 seconds</col>. You receive a <col=ffffff>1 minute grace period </col>when killing another player in a single combat zone. This is lost when logging out or teleporting.",
  PAGE3:
    "The Deadman's skull can be used to <col=ffffff>purchase sigils</col> and unlocks with <col=ffffff>Skull\u00a0Points</col> you earn. For every <col=ffffff>Deadman Point</col> you earn, you'll also receive a <col=ffffff>Skull Point</col>.<br><br><col=ffffff>Sigils</col> are powerful enhancements similar to League Relics. They provide XP boosts, combat boosts and other benefits. Some sigils are <col=ffffff>unlocked permanently</col>, while others must be <col=ffffff>attuned</col> to take effect. You can have up to <col=ffffff>three PvP combat sigils attuned</col> at the same time.<br><br>You can view the state of all sigils through the <col=ffffff>unlocks view</col> on the <col=ffffff>Deadman's Skull</col>. You <col=ffffff>can also toggle</col> those that allow it through the <col=ffffff>toggle section</col> of the <col=ffffff>unlocks view</col>.",
  PAGE4:
    "To help you get started, you'll receive <col=ffffff>60 minutes of immunity</col> before anyone can attack you. Speak to the <col=ffffff>Doomsayer</col> in Lumbridge to waive your immunity and get on with the killing!<br><br>Once you reach <col=ffffff>combat levels 61, 81 and 96</col>, you will need to move to a higher level bracket world. Each time you move up a bracket, you'll be granted a further <col=ffffff>60 minutes of PvP immunity</col>. <br><br>You'll receive a <col=ffffff>Deadman Starter Pack</col> which holds some handy items for you.",
  PAGE5:
    "Beware, at 02:00, 10:00 and 19:00 UTC, a <col=ffffff>Breach</col> will occur, where deadly monsters spawn. You can earn <col=ffffff>unique loot and Deadman Points</col> by fighting these monsters. You can check the next breach time through the <col=ffffff>Breach Check option</col> on the <col=ffffff>Deadman's Skull</col>.<br><br>Speak to <col=ffffff>Nigel</col> in the Lumbridge Graveyard if you seek further information.",
